text.section:
A corporation shall maintain the following records:

A copy of its articles of incorporation as currently in effect, and any notices to shareholders referred to in subdivision L 5 of § 13.1-604 specifying facts on which a filed document is dependent if those facts are not included in the articles of incorporation or otherwise available as specified in subdivision L 5 of § 13.1-604;


Its bylaws as currently in effect;


Resolutions adopted by its board of directors creating one or more classes or series of shares, and fixing their relative rights, preferences, and limitations, if shares issued pursuant to those resolutions are outstanding;


The minutes of all shareholders' meetings, and records of all action taken by shareholders without a meeting, for the past three years;


All written communications within the past three years to shareholders generally, including the financial statements furnished for the past three years under § 13.1-774;


A list of the names and business addresses of its current directors and officers; and


A copy of its most recent annual report filed with the Commission under § 13.1-775.
